course: dictionary
lesson: 5144
title: The iPhone: a brand and a warning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An iPhone is a brand of smartphone made by the company Apple. A brand name is a company's own name for a product, so it always starts with a capital letter: write «iPhone», not «iphone».
explain: «Click to claim your iPhone!» is a warning sign, not a good news message. The context clue is «claim», which means asking for something you have not earned. A message that asks you to click to get a free phone may be a trick to steal your details. Always ask: did I ask for this? If not, stop before you click.
explain: «The first iPhone (2007) combined a phone, camera, music player and internet.» In one device, that was a lot of different jobs. Some people say it «changed everything», but others argue about how big its effect really was. When you read a claim like that, ask who says it and whether they can prove it.
fact: An iPhone is a brand name made by the company Apple, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: An iPhone is a smartphone: a phone that can also take photos, play music and go online.
fact: «The first iPhone (2007)» combined a phone, camera, music player and internet in one device.
fact: Some people say the iPhone «changed everything», but this is argued, not agreed by everyone.
fact: A message asking you to click to claim a free phone may be a scam: check with a trusted adult first.
exercise: Which company makes the iPhone? | Samsung | Microsoft | Google | *Apple
exercise: «Click to claim your iPhone!» Why is this a warning sign? | It is a long, funny word | It tells you the phone is very old | *It may be a trick to steal your details | Phones are always free to claim
exercise: Which list shows what the first iPhone (2007) combined? | Only a clock and a calendar | A kettle and a toaster | A bicycle, a torch and a pencil | *A phone, camera, music player and internet
test: How should you write the name of the phone? | *iPhone | iphone | i-phone | IPHONE
test: Some people say the iPhone «changed everything». Is that something everyone agrees on? | Yes, it is written in the dictionary | Yes, it has been proven by a scientist | *No, people argue about how much it changed | It is a fact about dogs
exam: A message on your tablet says «Click to claim your iPhone!». What should you do first? | Click it straight away, before it expires | Send it to all your friends | Type your password so they can send the phone | *Ask a trusted adult and check before you click
